  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_01. Let quadrilateral ABCD be a 4-sided figure with AB = 8, BC = 6, CD = 10, DA = 12. Let quadrilateral MNPQ be a 4-sided figure with NP = 3, PQ = 5. ABCD is dilated to form MNPQ with scale factor 0.5, centered at point P. Find the length of MN in MNPQ.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A graphic designer is creating a scaled floor plan for a new office space. She starts with a detailed blueprint of quadrilateral ABCD with sides AB = 8, BC = 6, CD = 10, and DA = 12. To fit the plan on a presentation board, she reduces the design using a dilation centered at point P with a scale factor of 0.5, creating a smaller quadrilateral MNPQ.\n\nAfter applying the dilation, she measures two sides of the scaled figure: NP = 3 and PQ = 5. Now she needs to find the length of side MN in the scaled quadrilateral MNPQ so she can verify that all sides have been reduced correctly.\n\nWhat is the length of MN?"
}